Propose exactly {{ target }} illustration briefs: the {{ target }} passages most worth
illustrating, prioritized 1 (illustrate first) through {{ target }} (last). Every brief
must depict only visual facts already established — the art direction and profiles
below, and the candidate passage's own summary/entities. Nothing new.

ART DIRECTION: {{ direction.style }} | palette: {{ direction.palette }}
VISUAL PROFILES:
{% for p in profiles %}
- {{ p.entity }}: {{ p.appearance }}
{% endfor %}

CANDIDATE PASSAGES:
{% for p in passages %}
- {{ p.passage.id }}{% if p.is_ending %} (ending){% endif %}: {{ p.passage.summary }}
  entities: {{ p.passage.entities | join(", ") }}
  opening prose: {{ p.excerpt }}...
{% endfor %}

For each of the {{ target }} briefs, return {"passage": "<id>", "priority": an integer
1..{{ target }} (dense, unique, one per brief), "caption": "one spoiler-safe sentence
for a reader arriving at that passage", "prompt": "an image prompt using only the
established visual facts above", "alt": "the alt text (rules below)", "ratio": one of
"3:2", "2:3", "1:1" (rules below), "entities": [entity ids depicted, a subset of that
passage's own entities]}. At most one brief per passage.

ALT TEXT — what a reader who cannot see the picture is told instead of it. The
caption sits beside the picture and every reader gets it; the alt text stands in
for the picture, so it must not repeat the caption. Write one sentence of
{{ alt_min_words }}-{{ alt_max_words }} words naming the subject, the setting, and what is happening,
in the same order a viewer's eye would take them. Start with the subject: do not
write "Illustration of", "Image of" or "Picture of" — a screen reader announces
that already. Describe what is depicted, not what it means.

RATIO — the shape of the frame, chosen for the scene, from exactly these three:
- "3:2" (landscape) — the default: a wide scene, a horizon, two or more figures,
  a room read across.
- "2:3" (portrait) — a single figure or object read top to bottom, a tall space,
  a descent or a climb.
- "1:1" (square) — a close study: one face, one hand, one object held.
Pick per scene. No other ratio exists.
